WEBVTT
X-TIMESTAMP-MAP=LOCAL:00:00:00.000,MPEGTS:0

00:00.697 --> 00:08.372 align:center line:79%
For 50 years, I have studied culture,
including gospel culture.

00:09.206 --> 00:12.042 align:center line:81%
I began with fortune cookies.

00:13.644 --> 00:16.046 align:center line:81%
In San Francisco’s Chinatown,

00:16.413 --> 00:21.418 align:center line:79%
Gong family dinners concluded
with the fortune cookie and a wise saying

00:21.418 --> 00:25.856 align:center line:79%
like, “A journey of a thousand
miles begins with a single step.”

00:27.024 --> 00:31.328 align:center line:79%
As a young adult, I made fortune
cookies. Wearing white cotton gloves,

00:31.595 --> 00:36.400 align:center line:79%
I folded and tucked into shape,
the round cookies hot out of the oven.

00:37.267 --> 00:42.139 align:center line:79%
To my surprise, I learned
fortune cookies are not originally part

00:42.139 --> 00:43.640 align:center line:81%
of Chinese culture.

00:46.376 --> 00:50.881 align:center line:79%
To distinguish Chinese, American,
and European fortune cookie culture,

00:51.515 --> 00:54.585 align:center line:79%
I look for fortune cookies
on multiple continents—

00:54.885 --> 00:59.356 align:center line:79%
just as one would use multiple
locations to triangulate a forest fire.

01:00.357 --> 01:03.560 align:center line:79%
Chinese restaurants
in San Francisco, Los Angeles,

01:03.594 --> 01:09.766 align:center line:79%
and New York serve fortune cookies, but
not those in Beijing, London, or Sydney.

01:10.701 --> 01:15.339 align:center line:79%
Only Americans celebrate
National Fortune Cookie Day.

01:15.339 --> 01:18.709 align:center line:81%
[Laughter]

01:18.709 --> 01:21.244 align:center line:81%
And only Chinese advertisements

01:21.244 --> 01:25.048 align:center line:79%
offer “Authentic American
Fortune Cookies.”

01:25.182 --> 01:26.984 align:center line:81%
[Laughter]

01:27.751 --> 01:30.454 align:center line:81%
Fortune cookies are a fun, simple example.

01:30.721 --> 01:34.124 align:center line:79%
But the same principle
of comparing practices

01:34.124 --> 01:39.096 align:center line:79%
in different cultural settings
can help us distinguish gospel culture.

01:39.763 --> 01:42.866 align:center line:79%
And now the Lord is
opening new opportunities

01:42.866 --> 01:45.535 align:center line:81%
to learn gospel culture as Book

01:45.535 --> 01:49.206 align:center line:79%
of Mormon allegory
and New Testament parable

01:49.206 --> 01:50.941 align:center line:81%
prophecies are fulfilled.

01:51.975 --> 01:54.378 align:center line:81%
Everywhere, people are moving.

01:54.945 --> 02:00.250 align:center line:79%
The United Nations reports 281
million international migrants.

02:00.617 --> 02:05.255 align:center line:79%
This is 128 million more
individuals than in 1990,

02:05.522 --> 02:09.226 align:center line:81%
and more than three times 1970 estimates.

02:09.660 --> 02:15.532 align:center line:79%
Everywhere, record numbers of converts
are finding The Church of Jesus Christ

02:15.532 --> 02:16.967 align:center line:81%
of Latter-day Saints.

02:17.601 --> 02:21.938 align:center line:79%
Every Sabbath, members
and friends from 195 countries

02:21.938 --> 02:28.378 align:center line:79%
and territories gather
in 31,916 Church congregations.

02:28.712 --> 02:32.115 align:center line:81%
We speak 125 languages.

02:33.350 --> 02:35.152 align:center line:81%
Recently, in Albania,

02:36.086 --> 02:40.824 align:center line:79%
North Macedonia,
Kosovo, Switzerland, and Germany,

02:41.258 --> 02:44.728 align:center line:79%
I witnessed new members
fulfilling the Book of Mormon allegory

02:44.728 --> 02:48.265 align:center line:81%
of the olive tree. In Jacob chapter five,

02:48.532 --> 02:53.136 align:center line:79%
the Lord of the vineyard and his servants
strengthened both olive tree roots

02:53.570 --> 02:59.543 align:center line:79%
and branches by gathering and grafting
together those from diverse locations.

03:00.010 --> 03:04.514 align:center line:79%
Today, children of God gather
as one in Jesus Christ;

03:05.048 --> 03:10.053 align:center line:79%
the Lord offers a remarkable
natural means to expand our love

03:10.420 --> 03:13.623 align:center line:81%
and lived fullness of His restored gospel.

03:14.791 --> 03:16.893 align:center line:81%
Preparing us for the kingdom of heaven,

03:17.294 --> 03:19.930 align:center line:79%
Jesus tells the parables
of the great supper

03:19.930 --> 03:23.066 align:center line:81%
and wedding feast. In these parables,

03:23.300 --> 03:26.837 align:center line:81%
Invited guests make excuses not to come.

03:27.871 --> 03:31.274 align:center line:79%
The master instructs His servants
to “go out quickly into the streets

03:31.274 --> 03:34.411 align:center line:79%
and lanes of the city,”
and “the highways and hedges,”

03:34.411 --> 03:39.516 align:center line:79%
to “bring in hither” the poor,
maimed, halt, and blind.

03:40.317 --> 03:43.286 align:center line:81%
Spiritually speaking, that's each of us.

03:43.954 --> 03:49.292 align:center line:79%
Scripture declares: “All nations shall
be invited” unto “a supper of the house

03:49.292 --> 03:52.496 align:center line:79%
of the Lord.” “Prepare
ye the way of the Lord ...

03:52.496 --> 03:55.031 align:center line:79%
that his kingdom may
go forth upon the earth,

03:55.432 --> 03:58.201 align:center line:79%
that the inhabitants
thereof may receive it,

03:58.401 --> 04:00.771 align:center line:81%
and be prepared for the days to come.”

04:01.738 --> 04:06.643 align:center line:79%
Today, those invited to the supper
of the Lord come from every place

04:06.643 --> 04:12.449 align:center line:79%
and culture. Old and young,
rich and poor, local and global,

04:12.749 --> 04:16.853 align:center line:79%
we make our Church congregations
look like our communities.

04:17.854 --> 04:23.527 align:center line:79%
As chief apostle, Peter saw heaven
open a vision of “a great sheet knit

04:23.527 --> 04:29.966 align:center line:79%
at the four corners ... wherein were all
manner of ... beasts.” Taught Peter:

04:29.966 --> 04:35.939 align:center line:79%
“Of a truth I perceive that God is no
respecter of persons: ... In every nation

04:36.106 --> 04:43.079 align:center line:79%
he that feareth [the Lord], and worketh
righteousness, is accepted with him.”

04:43.079 --> 04:46.049 align:center line:79%
In the parable
of the Good Samaritan,

04:46.449 --> 04:51.454 align:center line:79%
Jesus invites us to come
to each other and to Him in His

04:51.454 --> 04:56.326 align:center line:79%
inn—His Church. He invites us
to be good neighbors.

04:56.927 --> 05:01.131 align:center line:79%
The good Samaritan promises to return
and recompense the care of those in His

05:01.131 --> 05:07.537 align:center line:79%
inn. Living the gospel of Jesus Christ
includes making room for all

05:07.938 --> 05:09.773 align:center line:81%
in His restored Church.

05:10.774 --> 05:14.945 align:center line:79%
The spirit of “room in the inn”
includes “no one sits alone.”

05:15.779 --> 05:18.548 align:center line:79%
When you come to church,
if you see someone alone,

05:18.815 --> 05:21.718 align:center line:79%
will you please say hello
and sit with him or her?

05:22.786 --> 05:24.554 align:center line:81%
This may not be your custom.

05:24.554 --> 05:27.858 align:center line:79%
The person may look or speak
differently than you.

05:27.858 --> 05:30.527 align:center line:79%
And, of course, as a fortune
cookie might say,

05:31.228 --> 05:36.566 align:center line:79%
“A journey of gospel friendship
and love begins with a first hello

05:37.167 --> 05:39.302 align:center line:81%
and no one sitting alone.”

05:40.637 --> 05:46.142 align:center line:79%
“No one sits alone” also means no one
sits alone emotionally or spiritually.

05:47.510 --> 05:50.580 align:center line:79%
I went with a brokenhearted
father to visit his son.

05:51.648 --> 05:55.285 align:center line:79%
Years earlier, the son was excited
to become a new deacon.

05:55.952 --> 06:03.526 align:center line:79%
The occasion included his family
buying him his first pair of new shoes.

06:04.728 --> 06:06.863 align:center line:81%
But at church, the deacons laughed at him.

06:07.464 --> 06:10.567 align:center line:81%
His shoes were new, but not fashionable.

06:11.368 --> 06:16.640 align:center line:79%
Embarrassed and hurt, the new deacon
said he would never go again to church.

06:17.674 --> 06:22.012 align:center line:79%
My heart is still
broken for him and his family.

06:23.747 --> 06:25.849 align:center line:81%
On the dusty roads to Jericho,

06:26.783 --> 06:30.720 align:center line:79%
each of us has been laughed at,
embarrassed and hurt,

06:31.087 --> 06:36.860 align:center line:79%
perhaps scorned or abused.
And, with varying degrees of intent,

06:37.360 --> 06:42.365 align:center line:79%
each of us has also disregarded,
not seen or heard,

06:42.365 --> 06:45.268 align:center line:81%
perhaps deliberately hurt others.

06:45.936 --> 06:51.408 align:center line:79%
It is precisely because we have been hurt
and have hurt others

06:51.775 --> 06:55.946 align:center line:79%
that Jesus Christ
brings us all to His inn.

06:56.846 --> 06:59.849 align:center line:79%
In His Church and through
His ordinances and covenants,

07:00.116 --> 07:03.586 align:center line:81%
we come to each other and to Jesus Christ.

07:03.987 --> 07:09.125 align:center line:79%
We love and are loved,
serve and are served,

07:09.426 --> 07:12.228 align:center line:81%
forgive and are forgiven.

07:13.196 --> 07:21.071 align:center line:79%
Please remember, “earth has no
sorrow that heav’n cannot heal”; earth

07:21.104 --> 07:25.475 align:center line:81%
burdens lighten—our Savior’s joy is real.

07:26.943 --> 07:29.879 align:center line:81%
In 1 Nephi chapter 19, we read:

07:30.547 --> 07:35.185 align:center line:79%
“Even the very [Son] of Israel do
[they] trample under their feet; ...

07:35.819 --> 07:37.087 align:center line:81%
they set him at naught. ...

07:37.487 --> 07:41.157 align:center line:79%
Wherefore they scourge him,
and he suffereth it;

07:41.324 --> 07:44.527 align:center line:81%
and they smite him, and he suffereth it.

07:44.561 --> 07:48.365 align:center line:79%
Yea, they spit upon him,
and he suffereth it.”

07:49.099 --> 07:52.602 align:center line:79%
My friend Professor Terry Warner
says the judging, scourging,

07:52.602 --> 07:57.440 align:center line:79%
smiting, and spitting were not
occasional events that occurred only

07:57.440 --> 07:59.342 align:center line:81%
during Christ's mortal life.

07:59.909 --> 08:05.448 align:center line:79%
How we treat each other, especially
the hungry, thirsty, those left out alone,

08:05.782 --> 08:07.417 align:center line:81%
is how we treat Him.

08:08.752 --> 08:10.320 align:center line:81%
in His restored Church,

08:10.320 --> 08:12.722 align:center line:81%
we are all better when no one sits alone.

08:13.189 --> 08:16.726 align:center line:81%
Let us not simply accommodate or tolerate.

08:17.127 --> 08:21.998 align:center line:79%
Let us genuinely welcome,
acknowledge, minister to, love.

08:22.532 --> 08:26.469 align:center line:79%
May each friend, sister,
brother, not be a foreigner or stranger

08:27.003 --> 08:28.738 align:center line:81%
but a child at home.

08:29.906 --> 08:33.710 align:center line:81%
Today, many feel lonely and isolated.

08:33.977 --> 08:38.081 align:center line:79%
Social media and artificial
intelligence can leave us yearning

08:38.081 --> 08:41.651 align:center line:81%
for human closeness and human touch.

08:42.152 --> 08:43.987 align:center line:81%
We want to hear each other's voices.

08:43.987 --> 08:47.323 align:center line:81%
We want authentic belonging and kindness.

08:48.458 --> 08:51.961 align:center line:79%
There are many reasons we may
feel we do not fit in at church—

08:52.395 --> 08:55.598 align:center line:81%
that, speaking figuratively, we sit alone.

08:56.633 --> 09:00.603 align:center line:79%
We may worry about our accent,
clothes, family situation.

09:00.970 --> 09:05.842 align:center line:79%
Perhaps we feel inadequate; smell
of smoke; yearn for moral cleanliness;

09:05.875 --> 09:09.079 align:center line:79%
have broken up with someone
and feel hurt and embarrassed;

09:09.079 --> 09:12.248 align:center line:79%
or concerned about
this or that Church policy.

09:13.283 --> 09:16.653 align:center line:81%
We may be single, divorced, widowed.

09:17.587 --> 09:18.988 align:center line:81%
Our children are noisy;

09:19.823 --> 09:21.224 align:center line:81%
we don’t have children.

09:21.958 --> 09:24.994 align:center line:79%
We didn't serve a mission
or came home early.

09:24.994 --> 09:26.496 align:center line:81%
The list goes on.

09:27.664 --> 09:32.435 align:center line:79%
Mosiah chapter 18 invites us
to knit our hearts together in love.

09:33.436 --> 09:37.107 align:center line:81%
I invite us to worry less, judge less,

09:37.373 --> 09:44.380 align:center line:79%
be less demanding of others—and, when
needed, to be less hard on ourselves.

09:45.115 --> 09:48.785 align:center line:79%
We do not create Zion
in a day. But each “hello,”

09:49.018 --> 09:52.222 align:center line:81%
each warm gesture, brings Zion closer.

09:52.856 --> 09:59.295 align:center line:79%
Let us trust the Lord more and choose
joyfully to obey all His commandments.

10:00.530 --> 10:04.501 align:center line:79%
Doctrinally, in the household
of faith and fellowship of the Saints,

10:04.868 --> 10:09.072 align:center line:79%
no one sits alone because
of covenant belonging in Jesus Christ.

10:09.506 --> 10:11.207 align:center line:81%
Taught the Prophet Joseph Smith:

10:11.274 --> 10:13.610 align:center line:81%
“It is left for us to see,

10:13.843 --> 10:17.714 align:center line:79%
participate in and help
to roll forward the Latter-day glory,

10:18.448 --> 10:21.284 align:center line:79%
’the dispensation of the
fullness of times. ...′

10:21.651 --> 10:26.456 align:center line:79%
when the Saints of God will be gathered
in one from every nation,

10:26.456 --> 10:28.958 align:center line:81%
and kindred, and people.”

10:28.958 --> 10:33.897 align:center line:79%
God “doeth not anything save
it be for the benefit of the world; ...

10:34.130 --> 10:37.734 align:center line:79%
that he may draw all
men [and women] unto him. ...

10:38.535 --> 10:43.573 align:center line:79%
“... He invited them all to come unto him
and partake of his goodness; ...

10:43.806 --> 10:47.277 align:center line:81%
and all are alike unto God.”

10:48.578 --> 10:52.448 align:center line:79%
Conversion in Jesus Christ
requires us to put off the natural man

10:52.448 --> 10:56.886 align:center line:79%
and worldly culture.
As President Dallin H. Oaks teaches,

10:57.153 --> 10:58.888 align:center line:81%
we are to give up any tradition

10:58.888 --> 11:03.293 align:center line:79%
and cultural practice that is contrary
to the commandments of God

11:03.560 --> 11:05.695 align:center line:81%
and to become Latter-day Saints.

11:05.895 --> 11:09.999 align:center line:79%
He explains, “There is a
unique gospel culture,

11:10.033 --> 11:12.268 align:center line:81%
a set of values and expectations

11:12.268 --> 11:16.940 align:center line:79%
and practices common to all the members
of The Church of Jesus Christ

11:16.973 --> 11:19.475 align:center line:81%
of Latter-day Saints.”

11:19.475 --> 11:22.345 align:center line:79%
Gospel culture
includes attendance at church,

11:22.645 --> 11:25.848 align:center line:79%
abstaining from alcohol,
tobacco, tea, and coffee.

11:26.282 --> 11:28.451 align:center line:81%
It includes honesty and integrity;

11:29.018 --> 11:34.123 align:center line:79%
understanding we move forward,
not up or downward, in Church positions.

11:35.358 --> 11:40.129 align:center line:79%
I learn from faithful members
and friends in every land and culture.

11:40.597 --> 11:42.865 align:center line:81%
Scriptures studied in multiple languages

11:42.865 --> 11:46.569 align:center line:79%
and cultural perspectives
deepen gospel understanding.

11:47.103 --> 11:51.341 align:center line:79%
Different expressions of Christlike
attributes deepen my love

11:51.608 --> 11:53.843 align:center line:81%
and understanding of my Savior.

11:54.344 --> 11:57.947 align:center line:79%
All are blessed when we define
our cultural identity,

11:58.281 --> 12:02.819 align:center line:79%
as President Russell M. Nelson
taught, as a child of God,

12:03.219 --> 12:07.357 align:center line:79%
a child of the covenant,
a disciple of Jesus Christ.

12:08.658 --> 12:11.628 align:center line:79%
The peace of Jesus Christ is meant
for us personally.

12:12.395 --> 12:17.834 align:center line:79%
Recently, a young man earnestly asked,
“Elder Gong, can I still go to heaven?”

12:18.601 --> 12:20.837 align:center line:81%
He wondered if he could ever be forgiven.

12:21.671 --> 12:26.943 align:center line:79%
I asked his name, listen carefully,
invited him to talk with his bishop,

12:27.477 --> 12:32.548 align:center line:79%
gave him a big hug.
He left with hope in Jesus Christ.

12:33.216 --> 12:36.085 align:center line:79%
I mentioned the young man
in another setting.

12:36.085 --> 12:39.289 align:center line:79%
Later, I received an unsigned
letter that began,

12:39.822 --> 12:45.228 align:center line:79%
“Elder Gong, my wife and I have raised
nine kids ... and served two missions.”

12:45.628 --> 12:49.832 align:center line:79%
But “I have always felt I would not
be allowed in the celestial kingdom ...

12:50.166 --> 12:53.436 align:center line:81%
because my sins as a youth were so bad!”

12:54.737 --> 12:56.539 align:center line:81%
The letter continued, Elder Gong,

12:57.106 --> 13:00.910 align:center line:79%
when you told about the young
man gaining hope of forgiveness,

13:01.544 --> 13:04.614 align:center line:81%
“I was filled with joy, beginning

13:04.614 --> 13:08.117 align:center line:79%
to realize that maybe
I [could be forgiven].”

13:09.118 --> 13:10.453 align:center line:81%
The letter concludes,

13:11.020 --> 13:12.889 align:center line:81%
“I even like myself now!”

13:14.657 --> 13:19.529 align:center line:79%
Covenant belonging deepens
as we come to each other and to the Lord

13:19.729 --> 13:22.999 align:center line:81%
in His inn. The Lord blesses us all

13:23.366 --> 13:27.203 align:center line:81%
when no one sits alone. And, who knows,

13:27.603 --> 13:32.809 align:center line:79%
maybe the person we sit next to may
become

13:33.609 --> 13:35.445 align:center line:81%
our best fortune cookie friend.

13:36.012 --> 13:42.085 align:center line:79%
May we find and make place for Him
and each other at the supper of the Lamb,

13:42.852 --> 13:47.023 align:center line:79%
I humbly pray in the holy name
of Jesus Christ,

13:47.357 --> 13:48.825 align:center line:81%
amen.

